 /spreadsheets/d/1xWFCPfY5m0aK9d5dnxvALNre-6-N7Cl0kkw24rvm6cE/\n\nCOSTUME
  / HAIR / MAKEUP for Trumpeter: Angels - Trumpeter — Costume (you prov
 ide): Fitted black shorts\, white fitted shirt\; Shoes: White ballet sho
 es\; Makeup: Men's Light Stage Makeup\; Hair: Neat\, out of the eyes/fac
 e\; Prop (BA provides): Trumpet\nLight Stage Makeup Instruction Sheet:\n
 •  Powder matching skintone\n•  Light brown eye shadow applied
  to the crease with an eye shadow brush\n•  Dark Brown/Black eyelin
 er and black mascara. No fake lashes.\n•  Blush on the cheeks (be s
 ure to apply plenty so dancer doesn’t look washed out in the stage lig
 hts)\n•  Red or Dark Red lipstick\nMen's Stage Makeup:\n•  Dar
 k Brown/Black eyeliner - apply from corner to corner\n•  Brown or t
 an under cheek bone to create shadow and accentuate the jaw line\n• 
  Brown eye liner around lips and nude/flesh colored lipstick\n• *Me
 n will not look like they are wearing makeup. It will help the face be s
 een from the stage.\nDancers of Color may wear flesh tone tights and fle
 sh tone ballet shoes.\nCostume Care Guidelines:\n•  Handle costume 
 pieces with care while changing to prevent damage to delicate fabrics\n
 •  Promptly notify Ballet Arkansas in the event of costume damage a
 t the point of discovery\, no matter how significant\n•  Never thro
 w costumes or accessories on the floor\, or hang costumes by their elast
 ic straps\n•  Refrain from sitting on the floor while in costume\n
 •  Do not attempt to alter\, mend\, clean\, or launder any costume 
 or accessory\n•  Never apply stage make-up while in costume and sha
 ll take great care to refrain from smudging make-up on costume during it
 s removal\n•  Refrain from the use of spray perfume or cologne whil
 e in costume\n•  Never wear any garment not assigned to cast member
 \n•  Do not handle or consume food or beverage while in costume\, w
 ith the exception of water\n•  Do not remove costumes from their as
 signed dressing rooms or from the theater\n•  Remove all bobby pins
  used to secure head pieces and wigs following their use\n•  Return
  all headpieces to their assigned bags\n•  Comply fully with any an
 d all updates to Ballet Arkansas’ wardrobe policies\n•  Do not pa
 ck markers\, paints\, colored drinks or anything that may damage or stai
 n costumes.
